<title>MEXICO: Sony de Mexico sees sales rising 60 pct in 1997.</title>
<headline>Sony de Mexico sees sales rising 60 pct in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sony Corp's subsidiary in Mexico expects domestic sales to grow 60 percent this year to $208 million against $130 million in 1996, Sony de Mexico planning director Juan Jose Regules said on Friday.</p>
<p>The expected sales growth will return the company to its 1994 sales levels, before the December 1994 peso devaluation, he told Reuters in a phone interview.</p>
<p>Sony de Mexico made about two million television sets in Mexico in 1996, of which 150,000 stayed in the country and the remainder was exported, the Siglo XXI newspaper reported.</p>
<p>((-- Monica Ballesca, Guadalajara bureau +523 817-0397))</p>
